thinking of. What are some of the practical uses that researchers are exploring for this? One that's gotten a lot of media attention is using it to communicate with locked in patients, people who are not able to communicate with the outside world, but may still be conscious and thinking. Is that research still ongoing? And are there other practical uses people are interested in? My colleagues, Martin Monti, Adrian Owen, several others have worked in that particular situation. The very clever strategy they came up with was if you have a locked-in patient, they tried to come up with mental activities that they thought would activate. very different parts of the brain, right? So it is that the part of the brain that's activated by

