and he scanned them multiple times over the course of the semester, and he looked at the brain patterns evoked by different computer science concepts and sort of how similar or different they were. And basically what he showed is that he could figure out how well a student knew a concept by basically comparing the similarity of patterns in the student to the similarity of patterns in the teaching assistant. And if this student had similar patterns when the teaching assistant had similar patterns and different patterns when the teaching assistant had different patterns of brain, that predicted that they would do well on tests of those concepts. Right, right.

